From 2cd687e74af6a1a49588dcaa8149de72f9f98440 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 07:56:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 35/36] Implement zxdg_output_manager_v1
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Thin wrapper over OwlOutput: logical_position/logical_size mirror
the same NSScreen frame values wl_output.geometry/mode already
report (owl applies no surface scaling beyond the integer
backingScaleFactor wl_output.scale advertises), and name/description
are deliberately not duplicated since they already live on wl_output
v4. Owl never tracks screen reconfiguration at runtime, so the whole
per-output object is static: the event burst fires once at
construction and no reference to the wl_output/OwlOutput is kept
afterwards, which sidesteps needing a destroy-listener pairing.

Global at v3, which deprecates zxdg_output_v1.done in favor of
wl_output.done — but only send wl_output.done when the client's
wl_output resource is actually new enough to have that event (added
in wl_output v2); otherwise fall back to the object's own done event
so a client that bound wl_output at v1 while requesting xdg_output
at v3 still gets an atomicity signal instead of silence.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VriRpmuZVKUEyysmR8WdJx
